Wait a sec: play()'s stop_threshold branch calls `self.next_question()`, which might raise ValueError (if the policy is exhausted), and that would happen before the try/except. Fix proposal: either compute the IG only when the policy is not exhausted, or move the stop check so it uses the try. An even simpler approach: restructure the loop as follows:

